A||N||7||Bugsy||Annoying Whining ||||5||
Z||000000||Bugsy||09-03-2000||10:47 PM||||Ok, i have this whining noise that sounds like a power steering pump thats low on fluid.<BR>I thought it was the alt. because its been going out for 3 weeks now, but today insted of showing a discharge, it redlined on me so i replaced the alt today...it wasn't near as bad as i was expecting.  Anyway, I assumed the whining sound was coming from the defective alternator, its starting to get annoying. Anyone have an idea where I should <BR>look for this noise maker? I'm hesitant to make the 200 mile round trip to see the kids<BR>TIA for any input <P><P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||5
Z||000001||MooCow||09-04-2000||12:54 AM||||Mine does the same thing and I had a friend of mine a mechanic look at my engine and he took a long screw driver and placed it on different parts of the engine to listen for a winning noise.  Well he pin pointed it and the whining that I have is on the left front part of the Plenum.(the thing with the Fiero written on it)  He told me to take that off and see what is under there making the noise.  I'm going to do that tomoorow so I will let you know.<P>                               Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||09-04-2000||02:42 AM||||There is nothing under the plenum that would whine, the only thing in the area is the Water pump and AC pullies. You might want to check out the water pump or AC which is in the same area but unless you have a whining timing chain or push rod (???)<BR>  Before you start taking off the plenum you might want to keep on looking for the whining!||||reg||4
Z||000003||Bugsy||09-04-2000||03:13 AM||||GRRRRR  I discovered that the whining quiets down as soon as I turn on the air. I suspect its the clutch on the compressor.<p>[This message has been edited by Bugsy (edited 09-04-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000004||Standard||09-04-2000||05:41 AM||||Hmmm.. I thought you were talking about that Northstar thread...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000005||myblack86GT||09-04-2000||08:23 AM||||I had that problem also. Check to make sure that one of the devices on the Alt. belt has not locked up. Sounds like it does have somthing to do with the A/C comp. Is it more of a whine, or more of a squeling? whining would most likely be the A/C comp. since it changes pitch when you turn it on.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bugsy||09-04-2000||05:49 PM||||It is definately a whine, It was a squeeler when I bought it, it was the alt the first time, I replaced the alt and the belt in April, at least the alt I put on it yesterday was a free replacement for the defective one so it just cost me time, not money.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Well, I guess time will tell. I watch my guages pretty close so if its the water pump I'll know soon I guess. I did check the pulley on the w.p. while I was in there yesterday, didn't notice any play. I have a feeling I'm gonna be in the market for an ac compressor.<P><BR>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin<p>[This message has been edited by Bugsy (edited 09-04-2000).]||||reg||1
